{
  "requirement": "Before drafting, the `habeas-requirements` skill MUST direct agents to ask the user whether uncommitted edits to the book that the agent did not make in the current task belong to the task.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "structural: The requirement text is: \"Before drafting, the `habeas-requirements` skill MUST direct agents to ask the user whether uncommitted edits to the book that the agent did not make in the current task belong to the task.\" It states no library, algorithm, signature, type, field, or delegation through a named interface. The only obligation is what the skill's text tells agents to do, and where that instruction sits in the workflow.\n\nI checked for a structural reading. Any wording of the instruction that tells agents to ask before drafting would satisfy the text, so the exact phrasing and file layout are discretionary.\n\nThe root `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md` does carry the behavior. In `section[Habeas%20requirements]/section[Workflow]`, step 1 (\"Check the starting point\") says to run `git status` on the book's source directory. It adds: \"If it has uncommitted edits you did not make in this task, ask the user whether they belong to it.\" Step 2 (\"Draft\") comes after it. So the instruction precedes drafting.\n\nNo implementation evidence for a structural obligation is needed. The behavioral obligation is met by the skill text.\n\nbehavioral: The requirement has one behavioral obligation. Before drafting, the `habeas-requirements` skill must direct agents to ask the user whether uncommitted edits to the book that the agent did not make in the current task belong to the task.\n\n`tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_requirements_skill_asks_about_foreign_edits_before_drafting]` is marked `{test}` for this requirement. It covers each part of the obligation:\n- It uses `step_of` to find the workflow step containing \"If it has uncommitted edits you did not make in this task, ask the user whether they belong to it\". `step_of` panics if no step contains that phrase, so removing the ask instruction fails the test. `workflow_steps` collapses continuation lines, so line wrapping in `SKILL.md` does not affect the match.\n- It asserts that the same step contains \"Run `git status` on the book's source directory\". This ties the question to uncommitted edits in the book.\n- It asserts that the ask step's number is lower than the number of the step containing \"Write drafts\". This enforces \"before drafting\". In `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md`, step 1 is the check (it contains the ask) and step 2 is \"Draft. Write drafts…\", so the real skill satisfies the ordering.\n\nThe test would fail if the ask were dropped, moved after drafting, or detached from the git status check. The requirement names no other modes, boundaries or failure cases.",
